ECISION: 'every successfully posted outbound Jira comment must have its returned comment ID recorded locally; divergence (post succeeded, local comment_ids unchanged) raises a bridge alert'","Plan step 3: 'a healthy observation (no posts, or posts with map growth) resets the counter to 0'","binding_lifecycle.py:512 record_comment_id grows the map per-entry, so a partial subset recording yields gained>0 while posted is larger","Original bug aa7b was total inertness (map EMPTY on Cloud), so the gained==0 proxy fits that incident but is narrower than the stated invariant"],"finding":"The divergence predicate ('posted>0 and comment_ids gained none') detects only TOTAL recording inertness, but the ratified design decision the ticket adjudicates is that EVERY successfully posted comment must have its ID recorded. A pass where posts land and only SOME record (gained>0 but fewer than posted) reads as healthy and resets the debounce counter, so partial recording failure — plausible under mixed DC/Cloud transports or a subset of no-op'ing entries — is silently invisible.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f73b1897ae80418","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / step 4 ('a healthy observation (no posts, or posts with map growth) resets the counter'); AC line 'gained none'","norm_id":"n54a1d9a93e958e00","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Mixed-transport clone: DC comments record (gained>0) while Cloud comments no-op; pass reads healthy, no alert ever fires","A single entry lacking local_comment_key no-ops while others record; the aggregate gained>0 masks it"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Define divergent as `comment_posts_this_pass > 0 and comment_ids_gained < comment_posts_this_pass` so a subset that fails to record is also flagged; keep the 2-consecutive-pass debounce over that stronger predicate.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","ass